  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "We can use input events like \"InputMoveHorizontal()\" or \"InputMoveVertical()\", but there's no \"InputTurn\" event.\n\nIn one of my worlds I use the event \"InputMoveHorizontal()\" to detect if the left joystick is used, but I recently noticed that this event is not fired if the player is in one handed mode (Which makes sense since the player cannot strafe in one handed mode, so I feel like having an \"InputTurn\" event could be an interesting feature). There are alternatives like  \"Input.GetAxis()\" but it can be pretty annoying to use them.",
